Checking platforms is how Our Dragonfly finds an exit. What happens if you change where the exchange happens?

A joke in a group chat puts you in front of an audience. A private message takes that audience out of the next move. A public thread may let you correct the record. A call may let you hear the tone you were guessing at. And sometimes the opening is to leave the reply box empty.

You can check platforms inside your own head, too. “I felt put on the spot” gives you more room to move than “I have to prove they meant to put me on the spot.” Same moment, different footing.

Before you choose your next move, check whether you want to make it from where you’re standing.